// The canonical Exsecutor program.
//
// It does not print. Printing is I/O, I/O is authority, and authority is
// declared -- so `saluta` returns the greeting and says, by declaring nothing,
// that it can do nothing else. `poscit` is absent because the empty row is the
// honest one: no allocation, no clock, no filesystem, no network. Whoever
// writes this to a terminal declares that capability themselves, and §10.3's
// audit will show it.
//
// Most languages open with a program that performs I/O. This one opens with a
// program that cannot.

publica functio saluta() -> textus {
    redde "Ave, mundus.

Ex silentio surgit forma.
Ex signo nascitur vox.
Ex codice fit lumen.

Hodie incipimus."
}
